        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6a981da3-5672-552f-b59b-96313c23ef1d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alberic II of Spoleto, Marozia, Hugh of Italy, Pope Sergius III, Pope John X\n- Places: Rome, Italy\n- Roles: ruler of Rome, Roman noblewoman, pope, king\n- Concepts: senatrix, patricia\n\nFacts:\n- Marozia, born Maria and also known as Mariuccia or Mariozza, lived from about 890 to 937.\n- Marozia was a Roman noblewoman and was alleged to have been the mistress of Pope Sergius III.\n- Pope John X gave Marozia the unprecedented titles \"senatrix\" and \"patricia\" of Rome.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto lived from 912 to 954.\n- In 932, Alberic II of Spoleto deposed his mother Marozia and his stepfather Hugh, King of Italy.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto ruled Rome from 932 to 954.",
